  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The Outbox write",
      "items": [
        "It builds each declared Snapshot or Tombstone from the prepared state; a mapper that changes anything fails the Operation.",
        "It records each Integration Event's <wire name>#published in the Module's Receipt store, so a second publication of one type fails.",
        "It writes one envelope per route, with the Operation Context, and each scheduled command with its due time; a message no route takes is left out."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Rollback",
      "items": [
        "A failed command or check rolls back and returns the command's Errors or the Operation's RollbackErrors; a change to another tenant's aggregate or to one attached rather than loaded, or a refused save, rolls back and returns its own Error.",
        "An exception at any step rolls back by disposing the transaction; one from the commit can leave the outcome unknown (ADR 0004).",
        "Nothing retries: a retry needs a new scope."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Around it",
      "items": [
        "The dispatcher starts the Unit of Work for the outermost command, after its authorizers and validator pass; a nested command joins it.",
        "A replayed request id returns its recorded success, and the steps after it find nothing to do.",
        "Without a messaging package there is no Outbox seam: the write and the flush are skipped."
      ]
    }
  ]
